# Citation File Format 1.2.0 (https://citation-file-format.github.io/). GitHub shows it as
# "Cite this repository". Validate after editing: cffconvert --validate -i CITATION.cff
# Add `date-released` and a DOI (`identifiers`) when the first release is tagged and archived.
# Keep `version` equal to pyproject.toml and src/jwst_anomaly/__init__.py when releasing.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file,
  including the version or commit you used.
type: software
title: jwst-anomaly-research
abstract: >-
  Open-source, reproducible system for ranking anomalous sources in public JWST
  data from MAST and vetting them against instrumental and known astrophysical
  explanations. An anomaly score ranks sources; it is not evidence of new physics.
authors:
  - alias: DD-Ching
repository-code: "https://github.com/DD-Ching/jwst-anomaly-research"
license: BSD-3-Clause
version: "0.0.1"
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - JWST
  - MAST
  - anomaly detection
  - reproducibility
